          "timestamp": "2025-10-02T13:13:06.448491",
          "sha256": null,
          "actions": [],
          "properties": {
            "operation": "create",
            "content": "# Configr Git Integration DemonnThis repository demonstrates the integration between Configr's File Module and Git Module.nn## Features Demonstratednn- **File Creation**: Using the File Module to create filesn- **Git Operations**: Clone, pull, and commit operationsn- **Version Control**: Proper git workflow integrationn- **Rollback Support**: Complete rollback of all changesnn## Files Creatednn- `configr-demo.txt`: Main demonstration filen- `.gitignore`: Git ignore file for the repositoryn- `README.md`: This documentation filenn## UsagennThis example shows how to:nn1. Clone a repositoryn2. Create new files using the File Modulen3. Commit changes to gitn4. Rollback all changes if needednn## Integration Benefitsnn- **Automated Workflows**: File creation and git operations in one configurationn- **Consistent State**: All operations are tracked and can be rolled backn- **Dotfile Management**: Perfect for managing configuration files with version control",
            "create_directories": "true",
            "status": null,
            "timestamp": null,
            "sha256": null
          },
